<header class="admin-head">
  <div class="admin-head__text">
    <h1>GitHub sync</h1>
    <p class="admin-head__lede">Everything published here is copied to <code>content/</code> in <a href="https://github.com/{{repo}}/tree/{{branch}}/content" rel="noopener">{{repo}}</a>, so git always has the newest version and its history.</p>
  </div>
</header>

{{#if (eq notice "ran")}}<p class="alert alert--success" role="status">{{icon "check"}}<span>Sync finished, the result is below.</span></p>{{/if}}

<div class="admin-split">
  {{#if enabled}}
  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="state-title">
    <div class="panel__head"><h2 id="state-title">Right now</h2>
      {{#if (eq sync.state "ok")}}<span class="pill pill--published">Up to date</span>{{else if (eq sync.state "failed")}}<span class="pill pill--scheduled">Failed, retrying</span>{{else if (eq sync.state "running")}}<span class="pill">Copying now</span>{{else}}<span class="pill">Waiting</span>{{/if}}
    </div>
    <div class="panel__body">
      <dl class="admin-facts">
        <div><dt>Branch</dt><dd><code>{{branch}}</code></dd></div>
        {{#if sync.lastRun}}<div><dt>Last checked</dt><dd><time datetime="{{isoDateTime sync.lastRun}}" data-local-time>{{isoDateTime sync.lastRun}}</time></dd></div>{{/if}}
        {{#if sync.lastCommit}}<div><dt>Last commit</dt><dd><a href="{{sync.lastCommit.url}}" rel="noopener">{{sync.lastCommit.message}}</a></dd></div>{{/if}}
        {{#if sync.lastError}}<div><dt>Last problem</dt><dd>{{sync.lastError.message}}</dd></div>{{/if}}
      </dl>
      {{#if sync.blocked.length}}
      <div class="alert alert--note">{{icon "info"}}<div><p>These files would be deleted on GitHub, because they're no longer published here. That's a lot at once, so it waits for you:</p><ul>{{#each sync.blocked}}<li><code>{{this}}</code></li>{{/each}}</ul></div></div>
      {{/if}}
    </div>
    <form method="post" action="/admin/sync" class="panel__foot">
      <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{csrfToken}}">
      {{#if sync.blocked.length}}<input type="hidden" name="confirm_deletes" value="yes">{{/if}}
      <button class="button button--small" type="submit">{{icon "sync"}}{{#if sync.blocked.length}}Delete them and sync{{else}}Sync now{{/if}}</button>
    </form>
  </section>
  {{else}}
  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="state-title">
    <div class="panel__head"><h2 id="state-title">Right now</h2><span class="pill">Off</span></div>
    <div class="panel__body">
      <p>The sync is off here because <code>GITHUB_SYNC_TOKEN</code> isnt set.</p>
      <p class="admin-row__meta">Thats right on your own computer. On the server, add a fine grained token with Contents read and write on the repository as the GitHub secret <code>SYNC_TOKEN</code> and run the deploy.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  {{/if}}

  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="how-title">
    <div class="panel__head"><h2 id="how-title">How it works</h2></div>
    <div class="panel__body">
      <p>One commit per batch of changes, a moment after you save.</p>
      <p>Drafts and anything scheduled stay here until they go live, the repository is public. The references list is never copied, it has private contact details.</p>
      <p>The commits end in <code>[skip ci]</code> so they dont redeploy the site. Pull before you push code yourself: <code>git pull --rebase</code>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
